english_question:
In the figure, it is known that AB is the diameter of circle O, and AD is tangent to circle O at point A. It is given that \( EC \sim CB \). Determine which of the following conclusions are correct: 
1. BA ⊥ DA; 
2. OC ∥ AE; 
3. OD ⊥ AC; 
4. ∠EAC = \( \frac{1}{4} \) ∠EOB. 
Among these, the correct conclusions are: (Fill in the numbers of the conclusions you believe are correct)

In the square \(ABCD\) with a side length of \(2\), there is an inscribed circle. A person used a random simulation method to estimate the area of the shaded part (the flag) inside the circle, denoted as \(S_{0}\). They randomly scattered \(100\) identical beans inside the square \(ABCD\), resulting in \(75\) beans falling inside the circle and \(25\) beans falling in the shaded area. Based on this, there are five statements: 
\(①\) Estimate \(S_{0}=1\); 
\(②\) Estimate \(S_{0}= \dfrac {π}{2}\); 
\(③\) Estimate \(S_{0}= \dfrac {π}{3}\); 
\(④\) Estimate \(S_{0}= \dfrac {π}{4}\); 
\(⑤\) Estimate \(S_{0}= \dfrac {4}{3}\).
Which of the above statements is incorrect? (Fill in all incorrect statement numbers)

In the figure, PA is a secant line to circle O. If PB = 2 and PC = 4, what is the length of PA?
A. 2
B. 2 \sqrt { 2 }
C. 4
D. 2 \sqrt { 3 }

In the figure, line l1 is parallel to line l2, and circle O is tangent to l1 and l2 at points A and B, respectively. Points M and N are moving points on l1 and l2, respectively, and MN translates along l1 and l2. If the radius of circle O is 1 and ∠AMN = 60°, which of the following conclusions is incorrect?
A. l1 and l2 are 2 units apart
B. When MN is tangent to circle O, AM = \sqrt{3}
C. MN = \frac{4}{3}\sqrt{3}
D. When ∠MON = 90°, MN is tangent to circle O

